 building your email infrastructure from scratch. The number one reason why most businesses are unable to grow is simply because they do not have a steady stream of prospects that are ready to buy their services. That's why in today's video, I'm going to be showing you exactly step by step how you can build a cold email system that sends a,000 targeted cold emails per day to your target audience without landing in the spam folder so you can get a steady stream of buyers begging to work with you and not have to worry about where your next meeting comes from. So, without further ado, let's dive straight in. All right. So, how to send 1,000 cold emails per day without landing in the spam folder. That's the important part because if you land in the spam folder, people aren't going to see your emails and you're not going to have a good time. So, the first question you might be asking is, Matt, how do I know this works? And to answer that question, I've done this myself. So, I'm currently sending thousands and thousands and thousands of cold emails per day over at my agency, Invo Marketing, for our clients, and have gotten results like these. 62 meetings within the first 60 days, 10 meetings and a closed deal within 10 days. All kinds of stuff here. And we've booked over a 100 salesqualified meetings for our clients just in the last month using cold email. These are people interested in wanting to buy their services. So you guys know that if you use this stuff and you actually apply it correctly, then you can get interested people wanting to buy your services and ultimately grow your business. So first thing I want to cover, sending more emails equals more leads. The number one problem that I see in most businesses today is that people don't know your business exists. You guys might have great products, you might have great services, but if you're not reaching out to people or doing any sort of sales activity to get in front of people's eyes, then they're not going to be able to buy your stuff because they don't even know you exist. So, one of the ways that you can let them know that you exist is by sending them cold emails and a lot of them. So, this is the craziest chart you've ever seen in your entire life. The more cold emails you send, the more meetings you will book. I know, crazy concept, but the principle is true. The more eyeballs you get in front of, the higher chance you're going to get someone who's going to be interested in your service. So, if you keep doing that sales activity, you keep sending cold emails, you're going to get people that are interested in your service just by virtue of getting in front of enough people. So, we're going to cover first how to build the infrastructure, how to make sure you're not landing in the spam folder, and then we're going to dive a little bit deeper into the different tools and how to make sure that you can implement this process inside your business. So, first talking about the sending infrastructure and the deliverability, how to build a cold email system itself. So, before diving into the actual servers and softwares and whatnot, one of the principles that I want to relay over to you guys about building cold email infrastructure and overall making sure that you don't go to spam is to make sure everything you doing is as human as possible. So, make sure your sending pattern is human as possible. And you just want to make sure your activity looks human. Even though we're going to be employing automation, the goal is to look human so that we don't land in the spam folder. So, diving into the actual tools and the different ways to set up email servers. So, you might have heard of different ways to send emai\n<truncated 356813 of 366709 bytes from the middle of the output>\nemailing and is trained on everything that you're doing and can make suggestions. It could write campaigns. It can give you best practices. It can give you health checks on your campaigns. Why aren't things getting delivered? what's critical about it. Like it gives you priorities on what you need to focus on and so much more. What else can we do? We can have generate a full campaign. We can write a sequence. Agency owners inviting them to my workshop and offering to send them a free operating system. What will it do? Based off of the memory, based off of cold email principles as well. It's not like it's needing to learn how to write cold email. It will generate me a cold email sequence. Pretty phenomenal. And from here, what I can do is I can see this. Not bad. Show me the emails. Not bad. So, you even give me the follow-up emails. Pretty killer. And I can even click on this and I can use it in a campaign and go ahead and pop it into whatever campaign that I want. Pretty sweet. Last but not least, I just want to talk about scaling with cold email. You might be like, \"Okay, cool. I want to like really scale this whole thing up.\" Well, really all we need to do is we need to rinse and repeat. So, what's where we rinse and repeat is with the analytics and optimization. So, your first step, let's get that first campaign out and let's see what we need to optimize. Is it the offer? Is it the subject line? Etc. We want to figure out what data points telling us so that we can know what to actually optimize. Do I need to rewrite my copy? Do I need a better lead magnet? Etc., etc. Then that will give us four different campaign ideas that we can then create for our same ICP that we can then stack these campaigns on top of to find the winner. So, how do we create the new campaigns? We build the list, we enrich the data, we write the copy using AI, we come up with a follow-up protocol, and we come up with a really banger lead magnet, and we're rinsing and repeating. And the other thing is is when people go through our campaigns, if I pull up my campaign for example, I can open up my campaigns and let's just say this campaign has been completed here, I can go to my leads and I can go filter by everybody who has completed with no reply. And then what I can do is I can export this list and add it to my next campaign. And I can use the new angle, the new test that I'm going with and continue to rinse and repeat and recycle. All we're doing is testing different offers, testing different call to actions, testing different problem awareness lines, testing different angles, testing different lists, testing different angles of list that we can get. Maybe we want to go for one that's location based. Maybe we want to go for one for people who are specifically SEO agencies who are specifically have this technology who are hiring for sales roles, etc., etc. We need to continue to reiterate on angles that we can then use for our cold emails which allow us to use that in the cold emails to increase likelihood of getting a response. But it all comes down to our analytics and it all comes down to our creativity. It all comes down to us writing really good copy, not burning it, not thinking, \"Oh, I'm going to send 10,000 emails tomorrow and get all these different leads.\" But no, being curious about this, being analytical about this, and being able to innovate and stacking. The most successful people, the people that are booking hundreds of calls every single month that I talk to, read the analytics, make improvements. They didn't start sending cold emails tomorrow and got all of a sudden got a bunch of results. They started sending cold emails. They analyzed it. They use different angles in the copy that they could come up with. There's no reason that you guys shouldn't do the same. And that's how you scale cold email. All right, guys. First things first, congratulations on making it through this entire course. That was a lot. Next step for you guys is implementation. But if you don't know what it looks like to actually implement cold email inside of your business, click on the video on the screen cuz in that video, I go from starting a business completely from